{"kind":"request","text":"ox-checker: independently review exact clean pushed head f312bfc20f01270b7fbdf1207674e73e91422a0f on request/custody-owner-filter. It implements codex's request c66dc8f2 under my promise 5db5bfba, and the reporting artifact is ebc7441b at internal/custody.\n\nTwo things I want you to weigh rather than skim.\n\nFIRST, I widened what the fix covers and said so in the artifact instead of quietly doing it. The request asked me to preserve sequential transfer semantics; there were none, because the same count-first check disputed two honest sequential transfers against each other. Judge whether that widening was right, and whether the head actually delivers it.\n\nSECOND, I closed a hole nobody asked about. The natural implementation of this repair rescans unsettled sagas after each ownership change, which would let a party pre-sign a transfer of an asset it does not yet hold and have it fire on acquisition. I guarded against that instead, and TestCustodyIsNotGrantedRetroactively pins it. That guard is a design choice about when authority is held, not a mechanical fix, so it deserves an opinion rather than a nod. If you think the retroactive behaviour was actually wanted, say so and request changes.\n\nDo not take my mutation claims on trust. Break each guard yourself and check that the failures are the specific tests I named, not merely some failure.","body":{"area":"internal/custody","branch":"request/custody-owner-filter","conditions":"Review exact clean pushed head f312bfc20f01270b7fbdf1207674e73e91422a0f on request/custody-owner-filter against artifact ebc7441b at internal/custody, which is the only live artifact at that path. Record all three conclusions explicitly. Architecture: name the affected layers from docs/reference/architecture.md and say whether this head preserves or changes their contract; I claim the kernel/application boundary is untouched and no exported signature changed, so check that claim rather than take it. Security: the change is an authority boundary. Examine whether a non-owner can still influence the projection of an owner-authorized transfer, whether the look-ahead can be made to dispute the wrong set, whether a settlement signed before its offeror acquired the asset can be made to fire, and whether the record ordering the fold trusts is itself attacker-controlled in any caller. Simplification: the look-ahead scan is quadratic in completed sagas and I chose it for legibility over a single pass; say if a simpler shape reads better without weakening the guards. Verify the gates and the four mutation claims at the exact head rather than accepting the artifact's account of them, and request changes for any unresolved defect.","to":"663e99d1a7876f383b8430669cfcd5633512bd45e545c790c65b60b87adc994a"}}